[gd_scene format=3]

; The Scriptorium, up the Undercroft's metal flue (map offset (223.5, 15.5)): a tall dry hall where Votaries
; kneel at lecterns, copying scripture onto plates; their bowing is the copying. The flue comes up through a
; hatch in the floor (Mag-grip from below); dropping back through it returns to the Undercroft. West, under a
; low vault: a pilgrim shrine and the first plate. East: a stair up to a gallery over the copyists (the second
; plate), then down past the last of them to the great tablet and the third plate. A dead end: lore and rest.

